  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThis loop over the batch size is inefficient and can be a performance bottleneck. It's recommended to use a vectorized implementation for better performance.\n\nAdditionally, the related function `compute_grpo_vectorized_outcome_advantage` appears to have the same numerical precision issue and would likely benefit from a similar fix.\n\n```suggestion\n        means = torch.stack([id2mean[idx] for idx in index])\n        stds = torch.stack([id2std[idx] for idx in index])\n\n        if norm_adv_by_std_in_grpo:\n            adv = (scores - means) / (stds + epsilon)\n        else:\n            adv = scores - means\n\n        # Handle numerical precision issues by setting advantage to 0 when score is close to mean\n        is_close_mask = torch.isclose(scores, means, atol=epsilon)\n        adv[is_close_mask] = 0.0\n        scores = adv\n```",
      "created_at": "2025-12-18T15:02:40Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -319,7 +319,9 @@ def compute_grpo_outcome_advantage(\n             else:\n                 raise ValueError(f\"no score in prompt index: {idx}\")\n         for i in range(bsz):\n-            if norm_adv_by_std_in_grpo:\n+            if torch.isclose(scores[i], id2mean[index[i]], atol=epsilon):\n+                scores[i] = 0\n+            elif norm_adv_by_std_in_grpo:\n                 scores[i] = (scores[i] - id2mean[index[i]]) / (id2std[index[i]] + epsilon)\n             else:\n                 scores[i] = scores[i] - id2mean[index[i]]",
